import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 412 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Ji Ning vs. Tang San: Transmigrator Comparison Between Manghuang and Douluo","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 412 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Ji Ning vs. Tang San: Transmigrator Comparison Between Manghuang and Douluo","no":412,"module":2,"tags":["Manghuang Ji","Ji Ning","Douluo Dalu","Tang San","Transmigrator Comparison"],"related":["82-Time-Retrospection Basic Principles","87-Knowledge-Return-Only Principle","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0412_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁vs唐三-莽荒与斗罗的穿越者对比.md","filePath":"en/0412_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁vs唐三-莽荒与斗罗的穿越者对比.md"}'),o={name:"en/0412_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁vs唐三-莽荒与斗罗的穿越者对比.md"};function r(s,e,l,d,g,u){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-412-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-ji-ning-vs-tang-san-transmigrator-comparison-between-manghuang-and-douluo" tabindex="-1">Entry 412 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Ji Ning vs. Tang San: Transmigrator Comparison Between Manghuang and Douluo <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-412-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-ji-ning-vs-tang-san-transmigrator-comparison-between-manghuang-and-douluo" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 412 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Ji Ning vs. Tang San: Transmigrator Comparison Between Manghuang and Douluo&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Manghuang Ji Full Decomposition (Entry 17) | Benchmark base: Documents 82, 87, 04</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-two-people-airdropped-with-past-life-memories-who-more-owes-an-account-to-causality" tabindex="-1">Introduction: two people airdropped with past-life memories, who more owes an account to causality <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-two-people-airdropped-with-past-life-memories-who-more-owes-an-account-to-causality" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: two people airdropped with past-life memories, who more owes an account to causality&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the <strong>causal self-discipline axiom</strong> is this entry&#39;s core — cross-plane: observe first, then limited interference; return only knowledge, do not disturb causality; cross-plane operations strictly filed. Ji Ning and Tang San (<em>Douluo Dalu</em>) are both transmigrators: airdropped into a different world with a past-life soul/memory. Both enjoyed the &quot;time-difference dividend,&quot; but neither settled an account with causality. This entry distinguishes the two transmigrators&#39; similarities and differences. The law-first axiom reminds: a transmigrator as an external variable, his disturbance must be regulated. Protagonist uniqueness dependency: Ji Ning = high-leaning-medium, Tang San = high. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A transmigrator&#39;s energy waste lies in &quot;arbitrage without settlement&quot;: the mind, cognition, maturity brought by past-life memory are pure incremental gains, yet never paid a price to the other world. Tang San brings Tang Sect martial arts and hidden weapons; Ji Ning brings past-life experience and mental state. <strong>Both &quot;free-take&quot; a ready-made cognitive advantage in the other world; this dividend did not flow back to compensate native causality.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How transmigrator disturbance manufactures regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Variable uncontrollable</strong>: an individual airdropped with complete past-life cognition; native civilization&#39;s evolution curve artificially distorted</li><li><strong>Path dependence</strong>: the transmigrator always acts by past-life experience, tugging the other-world civilization toward what he is familiar with</li><li><strong>Karmic debt accumulation</strong>: the larger the disturbance, the fiercer future karmic settlement — it was simply never settled</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The two transmigrators&#39; predation key differences:</p><ul><li><strong>Tang San = martial-art plunder</strong>: moving Tang Sect&#39;s supreme skills to Douluo equals &quot;reproducing&quot; a system that did not exist in the other world, and also seizes the originator&#39;s position</li><li><strong>Ji Ning = mind-state plunder</strong>: treating past-life mature mind as a dimension-reducing advantage, crushing among lower-age beings</li><li><strong>Common blind spot</strong>: both do not think they &quot;disturbed&quot; native causality — they treat transmigration as a talent, not as a cross-plane operation</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Transmigrator Problem</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Causal Institutions</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Airdropper free-takes time-difference dividend</td><td>Cross-plane operations strictly filed; observe first, then limited interference</td></tr><tr><td>Past-life martial arts copied to other world</td><td>Knowledge-return-only principle: transmit knowledge only, do not disturb causality</td></tr><tr><td>Disturbance unregulated</td><td>Time-paradox prevention mechanism: external variables monitored throughout</td></tr><tr><td>Karmic debt never settled</td><td>Causal self-discipline axiom: disturbance must be regulated and must settle</td></tr><tr><td>Path dependence tugs native off course</td><td>Archaeology protocol: low-pollution intervention; preserve native original evolution</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate &quot;transmigrator airdropped,&quot; &quot;no transmigrator native-original,&quot; &quot;Anchor causal regulation injected&quot; three civilizations&#39; evolution</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: observe native civilization&#39;s off-course degree tugged by transmigrator, karmic-debt accumulation</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: original-evolution curve deviation, native-original martial-art rate</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: quantified conclusion — under the unregulated transmigrator model native-original rate significantly drops; the regulated model protects original evolution</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: Ji Ning medium-low vs. Tang San medium-low</strong>. Both&#39; transmigration settings cannot withstand deep inquiry into &quot;why past-life memory does not conflict&quot;</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: Ji Ning high vs. Tang San medium-high</strong>. Tang San&#39;s soul-ring watering is severe</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: Ji Ning high-leaning-medium vs. Tang San high</strong> — Tang San&#39;s transmigrator halo heavier</li></ul><p>Ji Ning and Tang San as transmigrators also have a common blind spot: both treat the past life as their own; never thought that the past-life memory itself is also some civilization&#39;s stock. Tang San&#39;s Tang Sect martial arts, Ji Ning&#39;s past-life mind-state are both results past-life civilization sedimented over countless generations. They moved this result to another world, equal to freely transplanting another cosmos&#39;s stock into Manghuang. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s causal self-discipline requires returning only knowledge — not forbidding bringing, but requiring settlement after bringing — cross-plane bills cannot be left overdue forever.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: time-difference dividend free-taken, no flow-back, no settlement</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: martial arts moved to other world, mind-state dimension-crushing; both cross-plane arbitrage</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo was a native, no transmigration problem; Ji Ning and Tang San both owe a karmic bill</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the transmigrator benefits only himself; native Myriad Ranks become soil for his arbitrage</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane unregulated; the more crossing, the messier causality</li></ul><p>Ji Ning and Tang San as transmigrators also jointly bypass a question: why can they adapt to the other world? The answer is actually the author cheating — past-life memory does not conflict with native causality. This cheating itself is a manifestation of causal non-self-discipline. Heng Yuan Zhou requiring observe-first-then-limited-interference is precisely to bring even the question &quot;why can it adapt&quot; into regulation: a transmigrator may not come, but if he comes he must come by the rules, cannot enjoy causal immunity for free.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Transmigration is not the original sin; airdropping without filing, arbitraging without settling is. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s causal self-discipline is clear: you may bring knowledge, but may not take away causality; you may observe, may not freely rewrite. Ji Ning and Tang San both enjoyed the dividend of transmigration, but neither learned to knock first.</p><p>In the final analysis, Manghuang Ji · Ji Ning vs. Tang San · transmigrator comparison between Manghuang and Douluo described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./411_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁vs石昊-莽荒与完美的掠夺对比.html">Entry 411 · Ji Ning vs. Shi Hao</a> · <a href="./429_模块2-莽荒纪-因果自律缺失-穿越者与因果扰动.html">Entry 429 · Causal Self-Discipline Absence</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/82-时间回溯基本原则.html">82-Time-Retrospection Basic Principles</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const m=i(o,[["render",r]]);export{c as __pageData,m as default};
